| A membrane is an application's boundary when a host is holding it. Run on
| its own there is nobody holding it, and `Listen` says so.
|
| The alternative would be to answer `ok` and then never deliver anything —
| the same failure with the evidence removed. This is the line where an
| application built to be held finds out it is not.
link "native_modules/membrane.so" as door

| Configuring is accepted and does nothing: what a held application is
| configured with is its host's to decide, and on its own there is nothing
| here to configure.
emit Config { host = "127.0.0.1", port = 8080 } to door get c
assert c.ok

emit Listen { } to door get l
assert not l.ok
assert l.port = 0
assert not l.message = null

| And stopping answers `ok` either way, so one shutdown path works whether or
| not anything was ever started.
emit Stop { } to door get s
assert s.ok

| The vocabulary is net_server's word for word, so nothing else is here: a
| class this module does not handle is null, like any other recipient.
emit Whatever { } to door get nothing
assert nothing = null
